  "notes": "Cibak (Chibok) is a Chadic language of the Margi group. The orthography uses 'ǝ' (U+01DD) and occasionally 'ə' (U+0259) for the schwa. Complex consonants typical of Biu-Mandara languages are represented by multigraphs, including labialization (Cw), prenasalization (NC), and the lateral fricative 'thl' (/ɬ/).",
